Name: compileFromAST
Signature: struct NFA* compileFromAST(struct ASTNode* root)
Description: /**
 * @brief Compiles an abstract syntax tree (AST) into a nondeterministic finite automaton (NFA).
 *
 * Converts a regular expression AST into an NFA structure suitable for pattern matching.
 * Handles empty input, character literals, concatenation, alternation, and Kleene star nodes.
 * Returns NULL if the AST contains unsupported nodes or on allocation failure.
 *
 * @param root Root of the AST to compile. Must be a valid pointer to an ASTNode.
 *
 * @return Pointer to a newly allocated NFA on success, or NULL on error.
 *
 * @note Memory: Caller is responsible for freeing the returned NFA using destroyNFA().
 * @note Error: Returns NULL if the AST is invalid or memory allocation fails.
 *
 * @see createNFA, destroyNFA, isLiteral
 */
Dependencies: addRule, compileFromAST, createNFA, createRule, destroyNFA, isLiteral, redirect

